   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT authorizing New Hour for Women and Children LI, Inc. to receive\nretroactive real property tax exempt status",
    "basePrintNo": "S7543",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S7543-2025",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Real Property Taxation",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S7543\n\nSPONSOR: MARTINEZ\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act authorizing New Hour for Women and Children LI, Inc. to receive\nretroactive real property tax exempt status\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThe purpose of this legislation is to authorize the New Hour for Women\nand Children LI to file an application for exemption from real property\ntaxes\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1. Provides that the assessor of the town of Islip can accept an\napplication for a real property tax exemption from New Hour for Women\nand Children LI, Inc. for the 2023-2024 assessment rolls.\n\nSection 2. is the enacting clause.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nNew Hour for Women and Children LI is a not for profit tax exempt organ-\nization that owns real property located in Suffolk County at 248 Crooked\nHill Road, in the Town of Islip.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone to the State.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
    "multiSponsors": {
